[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64343,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In lobular endocervical glandular hyperplasia (LEGH), there is lobular proliferation of endocervical glands, often with pyloric gland differentiation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64344,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64345,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GA15.Y Other specified acquired abnormalities of cervix uteri</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64346,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64347,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64348,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LEGH typically involves the upper endocervix {18631191} and is confined to the inner half of the cervical wall {10435557}. It may be associated with multifocal mucinous lesions of the female genital tract {19207943}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64349,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may present with mucoid watery discharge.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64350,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present over a wide age range, typically in reproductive age.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64351,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64352,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LEGH can occur in patients with Peutz&ndash;Jeghers syndrome (germline <em>STK11</em> mutation) {23038761}. Sporadic LEGH can show mutually exclusive mutations in <em>GNAS</em> (42%), <em>KRAS</em> (5%), and <em>STK11</em> (10%) {24145653}. Atypical LEGH shows gain of 3q and loss of 1p, similar to adenoma malignum of mucinous type {18779726}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64353,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is most often an incidental finding or (less frequently) a well-demarcated mass.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64354,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A central cleft-like space is surrounded by a lobular proliferation of small to medium-sized glands containing tall columnar mucinous epithelium, sometimes with eosinophilic, granular cytoplasm and bland, basally located nuclei {10435557; 11683936}. Atypical LEGH is characterized by epithelial infoldings, tufts, or papillae, as well as by nuclear hyperchromasia, enlargement, distinct nucleoli, apoptotic bodies, and occasional apical mitoses {15143335}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64355,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Bland endocervical cells with yellow mucin on conventional Pap smears have been proposed as a clue to the presence of gastric-type mucin and LEGH {29982289}. A caveat is that the yellow hue is less apparent on liquid-based preparations.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64356,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64357,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> lobular growth of small to medium-sized mucinous glands surrounding a central cleft; atypical LEGH: epithelial infoldings, tufts, or papillae, as well as nuclear hyperchromasia and enlargement, distinct nucleoli, apoptotic bodies, and occasional apical mitoses.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64358,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 64359,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 296,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LEGH is a benign proliferation; however, atypical LEGH may be associated with adenocarcinoma showing gastric differentiation and is best treated as in situ neoplasia {28394803; 19723155; 23752085}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-04-28T15:01:32"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]